  "what_was_wrong_in_s1585": "s1585 serves with batched decode, which replaced the two-owner scheduler. The two-owner setup was also what switched on the response header x-native-execution-timing: v1 and the running/waiting stream comments. A router that leaves admission to the engine requires the header and refused every successful response without it, so no request reached a client through such a router. Requests sent to the engine directly were served; the release bar of s1585 sent every request directly.",
